- Dify (workflow/prompt orchestration)

## Single Widget, Three Phases
### 1) Setup Phase
Inputs collected: scenario, target language, level, user objective.
Server actions:
- Generate initial scene image (fal).
- Build NPC profile (name, personality, initial mood).
- Create conversation state.

Widget displays:
- Scene image
- Situation and objective summary
- NPC info and level badge
- Start button

### 2) Conversation Phase
Widget displays:
- Scene image (top)
- Scrollable chat log (middle)
- Hint button
- Text input + send button
- Give up button

Behavior:
- NPC responds in target language.
- Hints adapt to level.
- Image can refresh every 2-3 turns based on mood changes.

### 3) Debrief Phase
Triggered by goal achieved, failure, quit, or timeout.
Widget displays:
- Final outcome image
- Narrative summary
- 3-5 key phrases (target language + translation)
- Goal achieved indicator + retry suggestion

## MCP Tool Design
One tool: `parley`

### Input Schema
- `action`: `"setup" | "message" | "quit"`
- `scenario`: string (setup only)
- `language`: string (setup only)
- `level`: `"beginner" | "intermediate" | "advanced"` (setup only)
- `goal`: string (setup only)
- `message`: string (message only)
- `conversationId`: string (message/quit)

### Output Contract
- `phase`: `"setup" | "conversation" | "debrief"`
- `sceneImageUrl`: string
- `npcName`: string
- `npcMessage`: string
- `conversationHistory`: array of `{ role, text }`
- `hints`: string[]
- `debrief`: `{ narrative, keyPhrases, goalAchieved }` (debrief only)
- `conversationId`: string

## Server-Side State
In-memory map keyed by `conversationId`, storing:
- NPC profile and personality
- Conversation history
- Current NPC mood
- Message count since last image regeneration
- User goal and level

## NPC Logic (OpenAI)
System prompt includes:
- NPC personality and context
- User objective and scenario constraints
- User level adaptation rules
- Current mood state
- Safety constraints

Structured generation target:
- `npcMessage` (target language)
- `mood` (`skeptical`, `neutral`, `convinced`, `frustrated`, etc.)
- `goalStatus` (`ongoing | achieved | failed`)
- `hints` (level-appropriate)

## Level Adaptation Rules
- Beginner: shorter sentences, explicit phrase hints with translation, patient NPC.
- Intermediate: natural speech, lighter hints, moderate tolerance.
- Advanced: richer idioms/slang, minimal hints unless asked, stricter NPC.

## Conversation End Triggers
- Goal reached (e.g., mood becomes convinced) -> success debrief.
- Goal failed (e.g., mood becomes done/frustrated) -> failure debrief.
- User quits -> early debrief.
- Max turn budget (~15 exchanges) -> timeout debrief.

## Safety and Scope
- Reframe unsafe/illegal requests into safe communication objectives.
- Focus on de-escalation, dispute clarification, and respectful communication.
- Do not provide manipulation/coercion guidance or harm-enabling tactics.
- Enforce this in both scenario generation and NPC response prompts.

## Build Order
